# function runWith(use, x) { return use(x) }       main also passes a function that nobody knows: so flow does not list what `use` may be
# function looker(x) { x.n }
# function giver(x) { return x }
# function looks(o) { runWith(looker, o) }         the closure is made here: its function answers: a member is read, nothing is kept
# function gives(o) { kept = runWith(giver, o) }   the closure returns what it was handed, runWith returns that, and here it is stored
# function hands(use, o) { runWith(use, o) }       the called value is a parameter again: the row goes up
